Extent:
This law applies to England and Wales, except for certain parts.
Section 45(5) also applies to Scotland.
Section 19(3) and (4) also applies to Northern Ireland.
The following sections also apply to Scotland and Northern Ireland:
(a) Section 27;
(b) Section 29;
(c) Section 33(3);
(d) Sections 45(1) to (4);
(e) Part 3;
(f) This Part
The monarch can decide for any of the provisions of Part 3 to apply, with or without changes, to:
(a) Any of the Channel Islands;
(b) The Isle of Man;
(c) Gibraltar;
(d) The Falkland Islands.

