Sure, here is the simplified text:

Requiring a Bond: If, after investigation, it is proven necessary to maintain peace or good behavior, the Magistrate can order a person to sign a bond, with or without guarantors, as deemed appropriate.

Conditions: 
(a) The bond must not be of a different nature, larger amount, or longer duration than that specified in the order issued under section 130;
(b) The bond amount must be reasonable and not excessive, taking into account the circumstances of the case;
(c) If the person under investigation is a minor, only the guarantors are required to sign the bond.

